code of Life Data System (BOLD) (`coidb`, `coidb=221216`)\n- MIDORI2-CO1 (`midori2-co1`, `midori2-co1=gb250`)\n\n**nifH**\n- Zehr-nifH (`zehr-nifh`, `zehr-nifh=2.5.0`)\n\n**rbcL**\n- Diat.barcode - diatom rbcL, 263 bp (`diat-barcode`, `diat-barcode=15_2`)\n\nSeveral comma-separated databases may be given (e.g. `sbdi-gtdb,silva`) to run DADA2 taxonomic classification against each of them; one full set of output files is published per listed database. By default, only the **first-listed** database feeds every downstream step that expects a single taxonomy (QIIME2 filtering, diversity, barplots, ANCOM, R objects); use `--consolidate_taxonomies` to instead pick a per-ASV winner across all listed databases.\n\nPlease note that commercial/non-academic entities [require licensing](https://www.arb-silva.de/silva-license-information) for SILVA v132 (non-default) but not from v138 on (default). This list (including the exact accepted database/version strings) always matches `conf/ref_databases.config` -- supply an invalid value (e.g. `x`) to have the pipeline print the current list. See also the [usage docs](https://nf-co.re/ampliseq/docs/usage/#taxonomic-classification).",
